# Paper 1 submission source

Target journal: **Data Mining and Knowledge Discovery (DMKD)**.

The submission entry point is `paper1/main.tex`, using Springer Nature's `sn-jnl` class. The active text is assembled from:

- `sections/abstract.tex`
- `sections/introduction.tex`
- `sections/related_work.tex`
- `sections/overview.tex`
- `sections/implementation.tex`
- `sections/experiments.tex`
- `sections/conclusion.tex`

`paper1/latex/acl_latex.tex` is an old ACL-format draft and is not part of the submission build.

## Current evidence

The primary experiment is the paired KG-repair benchmark in `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/`:

- 1,499 clean/corrupted document-graph pairs;
- 2,998 manifested defects from six classes;
- document-group 70/15/15 split, seed 42;
- held-out test: 225 documents and 450 defects;
- shared model for Direct LLM, ReAct-style Agent, and Ours.

Ours obtains 0.9800 defect repair, 0.9932 clean-fact preservation, 0.0167 over-repair, 0.9917 triple F1, and 0.9333 exact graph match. The old corpus-level `Q_score` improvement of 8.89 points is retained only as auxiliary evidence.

The failure audit covers every unresolved test defect: 9/450, all in long government legal or procedural fields. There is no 150-case sampled failure claim in the active paper.

## Build

```bash
cd paper1
tectonic -X compile main.tex
```

The current build completes successfully. Submission figures derived from archived results can be regenerated with:

```bash
python3 paper1/make_submission_figures.py
```

Experiment details and exact reproduction commands are documented in `exps/PAPER1_EXPERIMENTS_OVERVIEW.md` and `exps/paper1_repair_benchmark/README.md`.
